---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { modelPolicyRecord as record } from '../showcases/model-policy/content';
---
<section class="model-policy-record wrap" id="saved-policy-check" aria-labelledby="policy-title" data-model-policy-record>
  <header class="policy-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">A saved source check</p><h2 id="policy-title">Same request.<br /><em>A different effective model.</em></h2></div><p>The explicit parameters meet the policy. A default role can still change what an agent would use. These actual hook outputs show why the configuration is checked too.</p></header>
  <div class="policy-request"><p>Identical request in both checks</p><dl><div><dt>model</dt><dd><code>{record.request.model}</code></dd></div><div><dt>reasoning_effort</dt><dd><code>{record.request.reasoningEffort}</code></dd></div><div><dt>fork_turns</dt><dd><code>{record.request.forkTurns}</code></dd></div></dl></div>
  <div class="policy-comparison" aria-label="Same request with two fictional configurations">
    <article data-policy-empty><p class="policy-condition">01 · Empty isolated configuration</p><h3>No default role to override it.</h3><div class="policy-result"><span>No denial emitted</span><p>stdout was empty</p></div><p>The hook returned without output. It emitted no explicit allow JSON, and no agent was launched.</p><p class="policy-process">Process exit <code>0</code> · stderr empty</p></article>
    <article data-policy-override><p class="policy-condition">02 · Synthetic default role</p><h3>The role selects Luna instead.</h3><p class="policy-role">Role model <code>{record.override.role.model}</code><br />Role effort <code>{record.override.role.reasoningEffort}</code></p><div class="policy-result"><span>Denial emitted</span><p><code>{record.override.hookEventName}</code> · <code>{record.override.permissionDecision}</code></p></div><blockquote>{record.override.reasonPrefix}</blockquote><p class="policy-process">Process exit <code>0</code> · stderr empty</p></article>
  </div>
  <p class="policy-disclosure">The original Python hook was executed offline with synthetic JSON and fictional configuration. No Codex, child agent, model or provider process was involved. This page displays the saved results.</p>
  <div class="policy-inspection">
    <details data-policy-method><summary>Source and execution limits <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><p>Unchanged Metacodex <strong>{record.receipt.source.tag}</strong> source, checked on 15 October 2026. Real user configuration and network access were hidden during the standalone execution.</p><p>The request names <code>{record.request.toolName}</code> and the active model <code>{record.request.activeModel}</code>. The two inputs were byte-identical; only the synthetic configuration changed.</p><p>Both denials exit 0 because the hook returns its decision in stdout JSON. The displayed reason is the exact prefix; the appended policy text is omitted.</p><p>A Codex installation must load, enable and trust its hook. That runtime integration was not tested here. This guard does not filter a model picker or text-only inference. The separate Metaclaude guard was not exercised.</p><p>The original 15-test suite result is historical; the suite was not rerun for this receipt.</p><dl class="policy-hashes"><div><dt>Hook SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{record.receipt.source.hookSha256}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Adjacent policy SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{record.receipt.source.adjacentPolicySha256}</code></dd></div></dl></div></details>
    <details data-policy-unknown><summary>A separate allowlist check <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div><p>One secondary input changed the requested model to the literal data value <code>{record.unknown.requestedModelData}</code>. The hook parsed that value locally; it was never sent to a model.</p><p><code>{record.unknown.hookEventName}</code> · <code>{record.unknown.permissionDecision}</code></p><blockquote>{record.unknown.reasonPrefix}</blockquote><p>Process exit <code>0</code> · stderr empty.</p></div></details>
  </div>
  <a class="policy-receipt" href="/media/model-policy/receipt.json">Read the concise source-execution receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
</section>
<style>
.model-policy-record{padding-block:40px 44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:24px}.policy-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:28px 64px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:28px}.policy-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,4vw,3.7rem);line-height:1.1}.policy-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.policy-intro>p{max-width:470px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted)}.policy-request{border:1px solid #adb8a2;border-radius:5px 5px 0 0;background:#f1f1e7;padding:20px 24px}.policy-request>p{font-size:13px;font-weight:550;margin:0 0 12px}.policy-request dl{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px 42px;margin:0}.policy-request dl>div{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:baseline}.policy-request dt{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.policy-request dd{margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--forest-dark)}.policy-comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border:1px solid #adb8a2;border-top:0;border-radius:0 0 5px 5px;background:#fbfaf4;overflow:hidden}.policy-comparison article{min-width:0;padding:25px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.policy-comparison article+article{border-left:1px solid #c1c9b7;background:#edf0e4}.policy-condition{font-size:12px;font-weight:550;color:var(--forest-dark);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px}.policy-comparison h3{font:550 25px/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 18px}.policy-comparison article>p:not(.policy-condition){font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted)}.policy-role{margin:0 0 15px}.policy-role code{color:var(--forest-dark);font-size:13px}.policy-result{border-block:1px solid #bdc7b4;padding:14px 0;margin:0 0 16px}.policy-result>span{display:block;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:var(--forest-dark)}.policy-result>p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 0}.policy-comparison blockquote,.policy-inspection blockquote{font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 20px;padding:0;border:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.policy-comparison article>.policy-process{margin-top:auto;padding-top:16px;font-size:12px}.policy-disclosure{font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);max-width:980px;margin:18px 0 24px}.policy-inspection{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.policy-inspection details{border-block:1px solid var(--line);align-self:start;min-width:0}.policy-inspection summary{min-height:56px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;font-weight:550;cursor:pointer}.policy-inspection summary :global(.ui-icon){width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0}.policy-inspection details[open] summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.policy-inspection details>div{padding-bottom:18px}.policy-inspection p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 14px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.policy-inspection code{font-size:.9em}.policy-hashes{margin:18px 0 0}.policy-hashes>div+div{margin-top:12px}.policy-hashes dt{font-size:12px;font-weight:550;margin-bottom:4px}.policy-hashes dd{margin:0;font-size:12px;overflow-wrap:anywhere;line-height:1.7}.policy-receipt{display:inline-flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;min-height:48px;font-size:14px;margin-top:12px}.policy-receipt :global(.ui-icon){width:18px;height:18px}.model-policy-record :is(summary,a):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:720px){.model-policy-record{padding-block:30px 36px}.policy-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}.policy-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,8vw,3rem)}.policy-intro>p{font-size:16px;max-width:none}.policy-request{padding:18px}.policy-request dl{gap:10px;flex-direction:column}.policy-request dl>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:112px 1fr;gap:8px}.policy-request dd{font-size:14px}.policy-comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr}.policy-comparison article{padding:22px 18px}.policy-comparison article+article{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid #c1c9b7}.policy-comparison h3{font-size:23px}.policy-inspection{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}}
</style>
